what does the Fast and Furious franchise  have in common with Shazam and what does  the inclusion of the daughters of atlas  mean for the future of the DC EU keep  watching for more details you may have  missed in the first Shazam Fury of the  Gods trailer 2019 Shazam was truly  something special the superhero flake is  dramatically different from others in  the DC extended universe and its sequel  is set to follow suit Shazam Fury of the  Gods arrives on December 21st on  Saturday at San Diego Comic-Con 2022  drawing Warner Brothers theatrical  presentation we got our first full  length trailer for The Shazam sequel  starring Zachary Levi in a red and white  spandex suit and his Shazam family the  trailer has everything you'd expect from  this film fun flying sequences mythical  creatures hand-to-hand combat and those  corny kinds of jokes that could only fly  in the world of Shazam Levi is back as a  titular hero with his foster family from  the original film fully suited up behind  him in their superhero form Freddie  Darla Eugene Mary and Pedro are ready to  take on villains hespera and Calypso  there were plenty of homages to the  original film and other DC EU flicks so  let's break down all the small details  you might have missed in the first  Shazam Fury of the Gods trailer Shazam  Fury of the Gods is upping the ante in  terms of adversaries for our titular  hero and his family the movie will see  Billy and the Gang go toe-to-toe with  two gun-like siblings in the form of  calypso and Hasbro who are collectively  known as the dorses of Atlas in the  first official trailer for the dceu  sequel they transfer Powers into their  beings by touching a magical staff and  it's clear that they mean business the  presence of calypso and hespera also  raises some interesting questions about  Shazam Fury of the Gods and the future  direction of the franchise could their  introduction mean that Atlas will make  an appearance as well the Titan has a  long-standing history with Shazam and  his Justice League compatriots in the  comics after all so it's entirely  possible that he's in the DC eu's plan  alternatively the movie might follow the  storyline in which Atlas is murdered by  The Wizard and his sister's mini one to  avenge their old man by causing Havoc  it's also worth noting that Atlas had  three daughters in the DC lore so  hespera and Calypso might not be the  only sisters to appear in Shazam Fury of  the Gods one of the comedic highlights  of the new Shazam Fury of the Gods  trailer comes when Shazam invokes the  famous family Motif that is Central to  The Fast and Furious franchise during a  budget attempt to summon the rest of his  own Shazam family as he sits down with  hespera over a bite to eat I've seen all  of the Fast and Furious movies lately  it's all about family the reference is a  funny one for fans and it's not the  first time a fast and furious joke has  appeared in Shazam but if you don't know  all of the movies you might have missed  that there are at least two strong  Personnel connections between these two  desperate films firstly shazam's family  speech is made to hespera who is playing  played by the grades Helen Miran Miron  of course has been a part of The Fast  and Furious franchise since that cameo  in 2017's the fate of the Furious she's  made subsequent appearances in her role  of matriarch Magdalene Queenie Shaw in  the fast spin-off Fast and Furious  presents Hobbs and Shore as well as  2021's F9 that gives shazam's Fast and  Furious reference an extra meta textual  twists that fans should find amusing  fans are also aware that another new  member to the Shazam world is also a  familiar Fast and Furious face Dwayne  Johnson who's set to make his DC  extended Universe debut in October 2022  with the Black Adam plays the titular  role of shazam's own arch nemesis and an  anti-hero capacity given that both of  Black Adam and fury of the gods are set  in the same sub-franchise of the DC EU  it's not Unthinkable that Johnson may  have some kind of cameo in Fury of the  Gods which is said to come out about two  months before the Shazam sequel hits  theaters further cementing the Shazam  Fast and Furious can action the Shazam  Fury of the Gods trailer doesn't give  away too many spoilers for thus we  should be thankful however some of the  visuals do tease some significant  expansions of the Shazam lore in the  dceu for example this image looks an  awful lot like the rock of Eternity and  this is a big deal with a cool backstory  basically the rock of Eternity is a lair  that is created by the original Shazam  who uses rocks taken from Heaven and  Hell in the comics a mystical Refuge was  used to imprison formidable creatures  including an entity known as the three  faces of evil which is a tri-headed  dragon that made life horrible for the  Shazam family if this is a rock of  Eternity we're seeing in the fury of the  Gods trailer and it does figure into the  film then it's entirely plausible that  the Apple mentioned the Delhi Menace  could be lurking in the shadows waiting  for an opportune time to plan a prison  break of course the lair also serves as  a power hub for anyone who's able to  channel the wizard shazam's  extraordinary abilities so the film  might not feature any three-headed  monsters it remains to be seen how the  rock of Eternity will be portrayed in  Shazam the fury of the Gods but his  inclusion will undoubtedly lead to some  interesting developments the newest  trailer for Shazam Fury of the Gods  shows our hero Zachary Levi Shazam as he  takes on Calypso and hespera after Ares  the god of war came after Diana in  2017's Wonder Woman this would be the  second instance of Our Heroes facing off  with the Immortals fans will notice a  little help comes for the villains in  the form of a dragon that emerges from  the ground looking as Fierce as anything  from Game of Thrones this is probably  the DC Comics version of lardon the  hundred-headed Dragon Atlas Center guard  the apples of the Hesperides while  missing all of its heads Ladawn CGI is  top-notch with the dragon looking like a  formidable opponent for the heroes as it  spits blue fire besides the dragon  viewers will notice another mythical  creature arrive on the scene near the  end of the scene of Billy Batson's  siblings ride black unicorns down the  street while they're all in their human  forms the Shazam family appears  determined as if their going into battle  the moment seems very reminiscent of  Trinity issue 18 where Wonder Woman  Batman and Superman are seen riding  unicorns on the Lost World Scott Taurus  we can't wait to see what other mythical  creatures will be part of Shazam Fury of  the Gods check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more Looper  videos about the DC EU are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the Bell so you don't miss a single one  thank you
 

